Receipt IV state and cutoff diagnostics — v1.0.1
Prepared October 2, 2026

Repair release: fixes the DuckDB MONTH alias syntax error in state preparation.
The diagnostic specification, cohort selection and account policy are unchanged.
It keeps the same private work root so completed input-authentication checks
are reused when the source-file fingerprints match. See REPAIR_NOTES.txt.

This package consumes the completed October 2 cohort assembly and the retained
November–January color replay. Run it once on the Mac with XT_Pro mounted. Both
__PRIVATE_VALUE_1__ and __PRIVATE_VALUE_2__ remain included, exactly as instructed.

WHAT THIS RUN COMPLETES

1. Authenticate the 16 completed analysis shards through their local READY and
   receipt chain. Require the reviewed producer, account policy and counts.
2. Authenticate all 15 retained November–January target-state Parquets against
   their exact hashes from the reviewed color result. Authenticate the five
   October 2023 checkpoints used for the fixed established-history labels.
3. Attach pregame RD to BOTH exposure participants. Check game ID, both numeric
   player IDs, speed, archive start, archive ordinal and both displayed ratings.
   Require all 468,029 missing primary recipient RD values to be restored, with
   no remaining missing RD for either side in the calendar-primary sample.
4. Preserve all 18,754,435 first-pair rows, the 3,917,764 calendar-primary rows,
   the 3,253,387 common-five/ten rows, all original scores and selection flags,
   and the 1,683,874 primary nonreachers. The same command resumes completed
   stages after an interruption; it never reruns upstream cohort assembly.
5. Produce calibration tables on the actual calendar-primary IV exposures for
   both player roles. Show all primary, fixed established and strict returning
   strata separately. Compare post cells to matched November pre-change cells.
   Preserve unmatched cells, color-specific signed errors, both near-zero draw
   gap sides and displayed-rating ties. No integer rounding rule is fitted.
6. Produce month-specific sample counts for a fixed grid of possible exclusive
   endpoints. Enforce anchor + 90 days < endpoint, preserving the original
   greedy spacing before applying any censor. Show the five/ten common sample,
   independently spaced ten-decision stream and properly supported lag-30 rows.
7. Verify the later-choice color interaction at the recipient's later choice.
   Nonreachers, unidentified choices and the implementation bracket remain NULL.
8. Save the exact mechanics commit/merge evidence and refresh the bounded,
   previously identified February source locations. Detailed paths and schemas
   remain private on XT_Pro. Presence alone is not denominator certification.

RUNNING IT

Save Receipt_IV_State_Diagnostics_v1_0_1.zip in ~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop.
Use the accompanying RUN_RECEIPT_IV_STATE_DIAGNOSTICS_v1_0_1.txt command. It verifies
the ZIP, extracts into a new directory, uses your existing project Python and
runs under caffeinate. No package installation or network access is needed.

Estimated runtime: 20–60 minutes on XT_Pro, not yet benchmarked on your Mac.
Allow at least 16 GiB of free drive space. Disk speed and spilling can change
the runtime. There is a 10-thread/worker ceiling and an 8 GiB configured budget;
two shard jobs run concurrently with five DuckDB threads each. This is a budget
for the configured databases, not a strict operating-system RSS limit.

There are no scheduled sleeps, prompts, artificial throttles or batch pauses.
Workers refill immediately. A heartbeat appears about every 30 seconds, with
an attachment ETA after shards finish. Reuse the same command to resume.

The run stops if authenticated inputs change or the required identity/count
checks fail. Such a stop produces an aggregate diagnostic ZIP when possible;
private tracebacks remain under the new work directory. Do not edit upstream
data to bypass a failed check.

WHERE IT WRITES

Private enriched rows and checkpoints:
/Volumes/XT_Pro/lichess_kindness/derived/replication_36m/receipt_iv_state_diagnostics_v100_PRIVATE

Private handoff:
READY_FOR_IV_SPECIFICATION_PRIVATE.json
This points to the enriched manifest and each authenticated analysis shard.

Aggregate output:
/Volumes/XT_Pro/lichess_kindness/output/receipt_iv_state_diagnostics_v100

Return bundle and SHA-256 sidecar:
~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop/RECEIPT_IV_STATE_DIAGNOSTICS_<UTC timestamp>.zip
~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop/RECEIPT_IV_STATE_DIAGNOSTICS_<UTC timestamp>.zip.sha256

Upload those two files after the run. Individual game/account rows, full
analysis shards and private source paths are excluded from the return ZIP.

WHAT THE RESULT MEANS

A successful result closes the missing-RD attachment dependency and supplies
the targeted calibration and endpoint counts. It is not a new IV estimate.
The mechanics deployment date, causal censor, announcement timing and final
later-choice control specification remain explicitly unfrozen.

The verified source change was authored/committed January 30 at 10:04:23 UTC
and merged February 1 at 10:31:02 UTC. Neither timestamp is a deployment record.
The January 30 midnight guard, source timestamp, merge timestamp and May 1
calendar endpoint are labeled sensitivity boundaries. No boundary is adopted
because it retains more observations or fits the behavior better.

The fixed-established label means >=100 same-speed rated updates through
October 2023. Returning means that label plus side-specific RD >=200 and at
least 90 days since that side's last same-speed rated update. These labels
affect calibration tables only, not inclusion in the original IV cohort.
Earlier returning-stratum history is not newly reconstructed in this package.

The three calibration strata overlap; do not sum them. Counts are player-side
updates when calibration is reported, and exposure rows when support is
reported. New/old payoff shifts are mechanical convention-based quantities.
They are not visibility estimates or grant-propensity instruments.

For the unconditional prospective IV outcome, nonreachers remain zero in the
inherited outcome definition. A missing later choice has no factual color.
Adding reached, later era, or later color as ordinary controls may condition on
post-receipt events; a missing-value indicator does not remove that selection
problem. NEXT_ESTIMATION_SPEC.txt lays out the remaining design decision.

No API pull, historical rating replay, chronology scan, score recomputation,
engine search, behavioral coefficient, first-stage F, IV confidence interval,
dependence-aware MDE or exclusion-sensitivity estimate occurs here.

VALIDATION

See VALIDATION.json and tests/test_diagnostics.py. Synthetic tests cover role
orientation, ID/rating mismatches, duplicate/missing target rows, preservation
of outcomes and selection flags, resumption, calibration matching, ties,
returning strata, cutoff boundaries, lag-30 support floors, nonreacher handling,
input mutation and author inclusion. The full Mac data are not mounted in the
development workspace, so no live sample or calibration result is claimed.
